" exrc: settings for vi(1), OpenBSD's base editor (nvi). The profile points
" NEXINIT here; nvi reads NEXINIT before EXINIT, so nvim and other vi
" clones never load this file. vi is the fallback: it is always installed,
" it runs as root and in single-user mode, and it needs no packages.
"
" nvi takes ex commands, one per line; see vi(1) under SET OPTIONS.
set showmode
set ruler
set showmatch
set autoindent
set iclower
set searchincr
set extended
set verbose
set filec=\	
set shiftwidth=8
set tabstop=8
